<article class="env-definition" id="02YQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02YQ">Definition <span data-tag="02YQ">80.3.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme contained in $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$. Let $F$, $G$ be presheaves on $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}/S$. We say a morphism $a : F \to G$ is <em>representable by algebraic spaces</em> if for every $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits ((\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf})$ and any $\xi : U \to G$ the fiber product $U \times _{\xi , G} F$ is an algebraic space. </p>
</article>